cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.'
title: 'IELTS API: a free, no-authentication REST API and open dataset for IELTS preparation research'
type: software
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  IELTS API is an open, dependency-free TypeScript REST API that exposes
  machine-readable IELTS preparation data: 4,174 headwords extracted from the
  Cambridge IELTS volumes 1-22 vocabulary lists, condensed analytic band
  descriptors for Speaking and Writing across bands 0-9, indicative score
  concordances for CEFR, TOEFL iBT, the Cambridge English Scale, PTE Academic
  and the Duolingo English Test, Writing and Speaking task banks, a curated
  corpus index, and six original fictional reading exercises with 36 questions.
  Reading practice includes stateless feedback, paragraph evidence, explicit
  matching rules and content hashes. Every endpoint is free of charge and
  requires no authentication. A per-file 100% statement, branch, function and
  line coverage gate checks executable TypeScript. The small reading collection
  has not been psychometrically calibrated. Cite the actual software commit
  and dataset hash used; no DOI or peer-reviewed publication is claimed.
keywords:
  - IELTS
  - English for Academic Purposes
  - second language assessment
  - vocabulary
  - band descriptors
  - score concordance
  - open data
  - REST API
  - TypeScript
